.TH adv
.SH NAME
adv - create and enter sequential exercise/task directories in a git project

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B adv
[\-p prefix] [\-w width] [\-n] [name]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B adv
is a helper function for working inside git-based learning or exercise projects.

It automatically determines the git repository root and creates a new sequential
directory based on a prefix pattern (e.g. ex0, ex1, ex2 or task0, task1, etc.) at root. (set-up instructions in README.md)

The function then enters the newly created directory and initializes a starter file
based on the selected prefix.

Directory numbering is determined by scanning existing directories matching:

.RS
prefix<number>
.RE

The next highest number is used.

If configured per-repository, behavior can be customized via associative arrays (see more in README.md):

.RS
ADV_PREFIX[repo_root]
ADV_WIDTH[repo_root]
ADV_NAME_REQUIRED[repo_root]
.RE

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-p prefix
Override the directory prefix (e.g. ex, task). Default is \fBex\fR.

.TP
.B \-w width
Pad numeric suffix with leading zeros.
For example width 3 produces ex001, ex002, etc.

.TP
.B \-n
Disable zero-padding entirely (numeric width = 0).

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.B name
Optional exercise or task name.

Required if ADV_NAME_REQUIRED is set for the repository.

.SH BEHAVIOR
When executed inside a directory matching the current prefix pattern
(e.g. ex12), the function first returns to the git root before creating a new entry.

New directories are created sequentially:

.RS
ex0
ex1
ex2
.RE

or:

.RS
task00
task01
task02
.RE

depending on configuration.

After creation, the function's will (behavior can be customized by editing `_adv_task`):

.RS
1. Enters the new directory
2. Creates starter files based on prefix
3. Opens them in VS Code
.RE

.SH FILE GENERATION
.TP
.B prefix = task
Creates:
.RS
main.cpp
.RE
and opens it in VS Code.

.TP
.B prefix = ex
Creates:
.RS
<name>.py
.RE
and opens it in VS Code.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Create next exercise directory:
.EX
adv
.EE

.TP
Create exercise with name:
.EX
adv sorting
.EE

.TP
Create task with padding disabled:
.EX
adv -p task -n
.EE

.TP
Create exercise with 3-digit numbering:
.EX
adv -w 3
.EE

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Success

.TP
1
Failure (not inside a git repository, invalid arguments, or directory creation failure)

